entries.body:
A correctness pass on the broker revenue page and the swap confirm screen:

• the revenue page now shows every fee asset, not just ETH — a USDG fee appears as 0.00081 USDG instead of “810 units of 0x5fc5…d168”, and the withdrawable total lists each asset;
• the broker list no longer misses a broker when an earlier one was fused away — the scan now covers the whole minted range;
• the swap confirm screen no longer shows “0” for a real, tiny fee — the exact amount is shown before you sign;
• nothing about where the money goes changed, and the page still reads the same contracts.

The Vault page has a new job: a daily curator bot checks this network for vaults, screens each one, and ranks them. Sparky then proposes the best pick — and a person on the team reviews and publishes it, so nothing reaches you unchecked.

What you'll see on the Vault page:

• Sparky's pick for today, with its net APY, TVL, curator and the reason it was chosen — always shown with the time it was measured;
• the full curated list, where each row says whether it came from the AI or an admin, and when it was last checked;
• an “Ask Sparky about vaults” button that opens chat with the question already typed;
• if there are no vaults on this network yet, the page says exactly that — no empty table pretending to be a market.

On fees: where SparkPoint adds its performance-fee wrapper, the fee applies only to gains above your high-water mark — never to a deposit, a withdrawal, or a flat or losing position. Vaults without a wrapper are deposited directly from your wallet and carry no SparkPoint fee at all. Either way, you sign from your own wallet and can withdraw directly at any time.

This network doesn't have a curated vault yet, so you'll see the honest empty state for now. When the curator finds one, the page fills in by itself.

The Swap page and Sparky got easier:

• the token picker now recommends the chain's real Stock Tokens — SPY, NVDA, TSLA, GOOGL, META, COIN, AAPL, AMZN, MSFT, QQQ, GLD, CRCL, RDDT and SPCX — each verified on-chain, and you can still paste any other token address;
• the “Route via” box is gone — Uniswap V3 is where swaps run, and the route still shows on the confirm screen;
• ask Sparky for a swap (“swap 0.001 ETH to USDG”) and the card now opens with the amount and both tokens already filled in — you just review and confirm;
• the SRK page links to its Pons launchpad, and the broker page links to the collection on OpenSea.

As always: you sign from your own wallet, and SparkPoint never holds your funds.

A pass over the beta's rough edges:

• the broker and revenue pages no longer run their labels into the numbers;
• the “partial data” chips are gone — a feature that isn't available yet now simply says so;
• Bridge is tucked away for now, SRK lives inside Learn, and the Changelog moved into Settings (all still reachable);
• no testnet or faucet talk anywhere — SRK is described plainly as a placeholder token;
• the broker page links to OpenSea and says the collection is a test placeholder.

Nothing about how anything works changed — this is clarity.

The beta is open at beta.sparkpoint.io on Robinhood Chain. Connect a wallet, sign a message to prove it is yours (nothing on-chain moves), and you can:

• chat with Sparky about your portfolio;
• swap ETH and USDG on the network's own Uniswap V3;
• if you hold a Sparky Broker, clock it in and collect its share of trading revenue — promote or fuse brokers too.

The swap charges the advertised 0.20% fee, and the confirm screen shows the exact amount and where it goes before you sign. Everything is non-custodial: you sign from your own wallet, and SparkPoint never holds your funds.

This is a beta — the token and the collection are test assets. Try it, and tell us what to improve.
